        <mxCell id="rD2CrnjHf7nBMmlK65hn-1591" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;## ERD Notes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;`erd-draw-io` is my original hand-drawn diagram (Catalog, User, Inventory, Orders), created in draw.io.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; color: light-dark(#000000, var(--ge-light-color, #ffffff)); font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;`commerceflow-erd.mmd` is the full system ERD (all modules). I used Claude (Anthropic&#39;s AI assistant) to speed up the work: it reviewed my diagram, suggested fixes, and generated the complete version.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;- I made the design decisions (scope, aggregate boundaries, relationships) and reviewed the output before using it. The design is mine; AI saved me the drawing time.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="250" width="1300" x="2710" y="1240" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
